Meeting status: Confirmed
This is an opportunity to influence: committee papers and any call for written evidence are normally published in the two weeks beforehand.', 'https://business.senedd.wales/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=986&MId=16303', '2026-10-12', '', '', '', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '', '16303', '', '2026-10-12', 48.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Legislation Committee; written evidence', 0, '2026-08-18T07:16:21.259843', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgWebService.asmx#GetAllMeetingsByDate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('14d0470fd3e6eeb5d3dd', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'Yes. Diolch, Gadeirydd. There actually used to be four. So, it puts it into context quite well. So, during the initial period of the Measures from 2007 to 2011, there were only four. There weren''t actually that many shortly after that—so, shortly after the referendum—and it was a significant issue for the Government at the time, because I think that, by that point, we were maybe five or six, and the other issue was that we were not very experienced. So, one thing I''d say about legislation, and I think most people would agree, is that it''s complex and it''s technically difficult and, as lawyers, there is a big difference between advising on the current state of the law and changing the law and taking responsibility for implementing policy and turning that into words on the page in relation to legislation. So, we''ve gradually increased the size of the office, and there is a proposal to continue that and to expand the office further.29

 One thing I would say is that it''s not as simple as just expanding the legislative drafting office. The Government as a whole contributes to the process. So, you have a number of people involved, ranging from the policy officials and economists looking at the financial issues, and lawyers obviously providing advice on the legal context and ensuring that what is done is done correctly within the legal framework. So, it''s a multidisciplinary process. At the end of that process, we come along to actually draft the words on the page, but there is quite a bit more to it than that.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dylan Hughes', '', '', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=717&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.165073', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770374', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('14d8d297488369cd3320', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'I welcome many of the steps taken by the Plaid Cymru Government since coming into power in order to address the real challenges facing the health service in Bangor Conwy Môn. We have seen a direct commitment to Betsi Cadwaladr University Health Board as well as additional funding for the health service in the supplementary budget. I''m sure that everyone would recognise the difference that that funding could make for patients and staff, and therefore how important it is that we pass the supplementary budget this afternoon. In looking to the future and to ensure that the good work can continue, we must encourage more efficient use of public funds within the health service. With that in mind, will the First Minister provide an update on the Government''s commitment to establish a health finance efficiency team and when he hopes to see that being established?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elfed Williams', '', '12165', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=2924&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.446582', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767550', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('156c1064da02a510010b', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'Are there any more questions from anyone? No. On behalf of the committee, I''d like to thank you all for coming here today. It''s been challenging, giving evidence and taking questions from the floor. We will send out to you the record of today''s meeting so that you can ensure that we''ve captured that discussion accurately. Again, thank you very much.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Carmelo Colasanto', '', '12152', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=7404&l=en', NULL, 103.5, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.768851', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769987', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('15c5662b62cae11c42db', 'committee_transcript', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', 'I was reading about the upcoming Cynnal payment scheme, so £10 for families on universal credit, per child, per week. I was interested to know, because, obviously, Reform had their conference earlier this month, and a big thing that Reform are passionate about is benefits going to British people as opposed to foreign nationals—. Obviously, Plaid Cymru are a nationalist party; they make a big deal about putting the people of Wales first. So, could we expect something like that from Plaid Cymru, where, if this Cynnal payment scheme''s going to be trialled, it could go to just Welsh people or just British citizens and not foreign nationals?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16247', '2026-09-23', 'Joe Martin', '', '12146', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', '16247', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16247?startPos=1941&l=en', NULL, 80.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'welfare_and_support; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee; universal credit', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.766695', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16247&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771164', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('15f201fb8a4dd490c785', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'May I add, Mr Thomas, that''s a crucially important question? Where the Bill that I''m involved in is in question, it''s my intention to ask the Bill team to connect appropriately and often with all the opposition parties, even before it''s introduced, to set out, ''These are our intentions, this is what we think, this is what the third sector says about this and that, what are your views, will you look at it?'' and so on, and to do so early on in the process, not later. Because the argument, very often—. It''s possible to make changes after a Bill has been introduced to the Senedd, of course, but it''s often better to have that conversation when there''s less pressure on people during the creation of that Bill.

 So, I''ve asked the Bill committee to be ready—and they''ve agreed—to go to speak to every party and, if I have the time, I will be participating too, on several occasions, I hope, in order to include everyone in the process. And that''s how I see things working. As my colleague says, of course, there are some Bills that we''re talking about now where, well, it''s likely, I hope, that there would be consensus.

 I hope there''ll be consensus on the tribunals, but to arrive at that consensus, we need to have that relationship, the conversation and the discussion, and for that to be a meaningful discussion—not a tick-box exercise, but to ensure that we listen to what the parties are saying, and so, in my view, develop better legislation anyway.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Elfyn Llwyd', '', '12193', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=1724&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.335197', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770377', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('1642b7eaee1da74cece4', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'I will raise my voice, Llywydd.

 Let''s be clear on the implications for additional spending on NHS waiting lists. We support these proposals. They are, after all, the continuation of the successful policy that the last Welsh Government adopted. You do not need a supplementary budget in place to spend in this area. You can carry on the investment now and regularise that spend later in the year. Fearmongering that this money is at risk simply does not bear informed scrutiny.

 And as to the suggestion that if the supplementary budget failed, there would be no money given to ALN at a later date, if that''s accurate then it''s pernicious, it''s vindictive and it''s going to lead to widespread industrial action. The supplementary budget before us has £0.25 billion of unallocated financial resources. I''ve outlined before, the Chair of the Finance Committee has repeated it: that''s not normal. You could use £100 million, as we''ve requested for ALN, and still have a substantial cushion to manage in-year spending pressures.

 Llywydd, we genuinely tried to warn the Government that they were headed for the rocks. My advice now is just as genuine: withdraw the supplementary budget today, negotiate with the teaching unions to resolve this dispute you''ve blundered into, and then bring back a supplementary budget that actually starts to meet the asks of pupils and teachers. When you do, we''ll be here waiting, ready to vote for it. Diolch yn fawr.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Thomas', '', '12156', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=24201&l=en', NULL, 49.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context; committee_scrutiny', 'Context; Housing system', '', '', 'Finance Committee; supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.612649', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767897', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('167230e2d3ab0c97b049', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'Me again? [ Laughter .] I think the frequency—. The flexibility in the regs does allow EROs some idea of timing an AVR exercise that might suit their circumstances and their type of local authority area better. I would say that AVR isn''t the only mechanism that the electoral registration officers have to get people on the register. We already do quite a lot of work, and I think this is pretty much commonplace across local authority areas. We regularly receive updates from our council tax team with regard to movers coming into the authority, account changes, and most electoral registration officers and teams would be fairly proactive in reaching out to those individuals and encouraging them to register because they''ve moved address and, therefore, they will have, potentially, lost their right to vote at their last address. So, I think electoral registration teams have got quite good at becoming proactive and chasing up changes to addresses. So, I would say that AVR isn''t the only mechanism we have to get these people registered. Obviously, it does require a little bit more input from those individuals themselves.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Sandra Matthews', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=4996&l=en', NULL, 109.2, 'High', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Tax & finance', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; council tax; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.353066', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769950', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('16c263fca60cb087d583', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'I thank the Member for drawing attention to the genuine pressure that exists, which is caused by childcare costs. Even though my children are getting older now, I remember clearly the heavy costs involved in providing childcare, and we as a Government are determined to help, with regard to the financial costs, the opportunities given to children, and the economic opportunities that follow for parents and so forth.

 The Deputy First Minister will provide an update to the Senedd today on the process of rolling out the childcare offer, as well as information on the cost modelling. The additional investment through the supplementary budget is going to allow us to expand thousands of additional funded childcare places, focusing immediately on expanding childcare for two-year-olds. This is always something that happens in phases: the 12.5 hours, the 20 hours, and then onwards to the youngest children. That''s how it''s planned, to increase the financial envelope and the workforce at the same time. But we''re clear that this transformational change requires a childcare sector that is strong and sustainable, a skilled workforce, and a budget that works for providers as well as parents.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=3302&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.481769', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767536', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('17a0826ebfda2b217fbd', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'I tell you what, Llywydd, if the Member thinks you can only do one thing at a time in Government, she should give up her aspirations right now, because it is all about dealing with a host of issues that are in the interests of building our nation. It is about doing the work that we''ve done over the summer to pump money into health and to change our attitude on how we bring those waiting times down. It is about the numeracy and literacy strategy that is being published today by my Minister for education. And when it comes to this pursuit of more powers, which Reform absolutely rejects, let''s remind the Member that it''s because of powers taken on around a decade ago over non-domestic rates that we are now able to make a positive decision to help businesses in Wales through a cut of a third in the rates for businesses in hospitality and leisure. We have our eyes on the future of Wales, and I suggest that the Member opposite does the same.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16260', '2026-09-15', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16260', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16260?startPos=976&l=en', NULL, 60.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'non-domestic rates', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:24.966630', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16260&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768990', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('181474e8f30e7045828d', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Well, look, we found ourselves, post Brexit, in a situation where we didn''t have that environmental governance oversight. It was a vacuum that needed to be filled. Other parts of the UK filled it. And regrettably, we didn''t get to the point where we had that body in as timely a manner as we would have wished. We''re now getting to a position where that is in place. And it will be a key part in that ecosystem, if you like, in terms of having that oversight on Government and others. And it''s one element, I think, in a bigger picture here, because we will have the statutory targets for biodiversity coming on board. Work has already started on that as a consequence of legislation passed in the last Senedd. And as somebody who sat over there arguing for strong and meaningful targets, we will make sure that that is the case. And as somebody also who sat over there arguing for the environmental governance body to have teeth, I will make sure that that is the case as well. So, there''s a lot happening. Rhodri, do you want to add anything on that?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=2835&l=en', NULL, 34.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:34.709782', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#772000', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('184f710f10433904848e', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', 'Yes. Thank you, Chair. Good morning, both. Thank you for joining us this morning. It is an important area that we need to discover. I suppose, if I could start with some of your thoughts on the evaluation of the pilots and just, really, if you could help us understand the main challenges you''ve found, through the pilots, to delivering automatic voter registration effectively. What are they likely to be for us?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Peter Fox', '', '4787', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=156&l=en', NULL, 97.7, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Opposition housing leads', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:48.702076', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769807', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('186263c59a5f60861833', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'No, no, you''re the expert. [ Laughter .]', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=6322&l=en', NULL, 34.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.151053', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#772121', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('1869449e69298b3cf6b8', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Thank you for that full and comprehensive answer, Richard. Cabinet Secretary.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'James Evans', '', '8585', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=5804&l=en', NULL, 46.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Other committee chairs', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.071022', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#772062', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('189105299d3dd29c74db', 'committee_transcript', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', 'Thank you. I think that what Joe was maybe clunkily referring to is positive action that''s being taken to tackle barriers to equality. So, I''d be really keen to hear what actions the Welsh Government is taking to tackle gender inequality and whether you have—I''m not sure whether it comes into your portfolio—had any evaluation of—it was quite delayed—the previous work that the Welsh Government did on gender budgeting pilots and to see if that will be taken forward at all.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16247', '2026-09-23', 'Sarah Rees', '', '5196', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', '16247', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16247?startPos=4309&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.989947', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16247&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771294', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('189581ac0a90d7e360d8', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'Thank you, David. Elyn.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Carmelo Colasanto', '', '12152', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=5547&l=en', NULL, 103.5, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.444879', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770015', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
