Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Consultation: Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Issue Details Issue History Related Meetings The forward work programme of the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee sets out the work which the Committee is intending to carry out in the following weeks and months. Any documents published indicate the current intentions of the Committee at the time of publishing, however the programme may change at any time to respond to external events. ¬¬¬ Consultation: Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee The Committee is seeking views from people and organisations on the issues they believe it should prioritise in the Seventh Senedd. Further information on how to submit your views is available on the consultation page . zzz Business type: Other First published: 15/06/2026 Consultations Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee (running until 11/09/2026) Topics Helpful Links Find a Member of the Senedd chevron_right Sign up to updates from Senedd committees chevron_right Senedd Now chevron_right Glossary chevron_right Related No results were found', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47576', '2026-08-04', '', '', '', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '', '', '', NULL, 98.0, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Consultation open', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee; consultation; consultations; seeking views', 0, '2026-08-04T14:02:45.848130', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47576', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('35483b1537a1ec6f145d', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', 'Thank you. Elyn, you''ve actually got the next question: availability and quality of data.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Carmelo Colasanto', '', '12152', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=2121&l=en', NULL, 103.5, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.013800', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769844', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('356bfcb9d5b727bd036b', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'It was like you read my mind then; I was going to ask how confident you are of the capacity to deal with legislative consent memorandums. But I''ll just finish with if you''re able to provide any expected balance between primary and secondary legislation over this term at all.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Kiera Marshall', '', '12166', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=1183&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.241393', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770356', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('35943d7b579c36c5b8c6', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'Brif Weinidog, private renting has become increasingly unaffordable, with many households now spending a really unsustainable amount of their income simply on keeping a roof over their heads. Recent Citizens Advice data has shown that some people are spending up to 70 per cent of their income on rent alone, and in Cardiff, there are instances of rents more than doubling now, with just two months'' notice. As a consequence, homelessness services are facing increased demand, not only because people are being evicted from their homes, but because council support with rent is also insufficient, placing greater pressure on social housing and temporary accommodation. Does the First Minister agree with me that spending more than two thirds of an individual''s income on rent is not acceptable, and that limiting annual rent increases is essential?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16260', '2026-09-15', 'Zaynub Akbar', '', '12141', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16260', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16260?startPos=2282&l=en', NULL, 187.0, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'rent_controls_and_affordability; evictions_and_possession; homelessness; social_housing', 'Housing system; Private rented sector', 'First Minister / Cabinet; Other committee chairs', '', 'evicted; homelessness; rent increases; social housing; temporary accommodation', 0, '2026-09-16T11:53:07.215763', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16260&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769018', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('35e850c79f780fcaee2f', 'committee_transcript', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', 'We''re always keen to get dates in due course. It sounds like way down the line, but, yes, it''d be good for us as a committee to maybe follow the work that you''re doing on that point as well. So, I''d be very grateful if we can follow that. It''s really important work.

 You mentioned tackling misinformation and I think that''s absolutely crucial. We''ve touched on social media, haven''t we? But there''s so much around trying to get in quite early around that misinformation that can easily get around and really cause some community cohesion issues.

 I know that, on a different scale, the UK Government announced today a new agency that''s going to be established. And I''m just wondering, this isn''t just—. Obviously, this will be a cross-Government responsibility about how we tackle misinformation. I''m just wondering what more we can do, what you''re doing in that space as well, and how you can bring people together to make sure we''re tackling misinformation at source as effectively as possible.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16247', '2026-09-23', 'Jayne Bryant', '', '5038', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', '16247', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16247?startPos=6134&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet; Opposition housing leads', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:36.199882', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16247&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771260', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('35f84869d6cf8313e210', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'Yes, thank you.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Rebeca Phillips', '', '12172', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=6473&l=en', NULL, 103.5, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.608773', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769976', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('36a45b80f6908a8c061f', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'Sophie might speak to that.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dafydd Trystan Davies', '', '12140', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=2522&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.511022', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770451', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('36a638eb6e90f5dd172e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'Of course, my Government will do everything we can and already have done to support those who are affected by these fires. My thanks initially go to the people who responded to them. My thoughts are with the people who are affected by them.

 On the question of a Minister for north Wales, I have a Minister for north Wales. It''s Siân Gwenllian, and it''s Dafydd Trystan, and it''s Anna Brychan, it''s Mabon ap Gwynfor, it''s Sioned Williams—all my Ministers are Ministers for all of Wales. Where was Labour''s Minister for the south of Wales, if that matters? Because all my Ministers are Ministers for the south of Wales too, and the west of Wales, and mid Wales, because we are a joined-up Government that has a plan for our nation—all of our nation.

 That is why all of us have come together around this supplementary budget today—north, south, east, west, and mid, it''s important to remember—with a determination to change the lives of the people of Wales for the better. We have a supplementary budget that is focused on making the NHS sustainable. I will be voting for that sustainability for the NHS. The leader of Labour in Wales is threatening to vote against that. I will be voting for expanding free school meals under this supplementary budget. The Labour leader here is threatening to vote against that. I will be voting for the expansion of paid-for childcare in Wales. The Labour leader threatens to vote against that. And, yes, I will be voting for a package worth £120 million for ALN that he and I negotiated positively on, and he is threatening to vote to not allow that spending to go ahead. This is a Government for all of Wales with a vision for all of our nation.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=1314&l=en', NULL, 71.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'Housing minister; First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.311408', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767509', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
