Forward work programme – Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Forward work programme – Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Consultation: Priorities Consultation: Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Issue Details Related Meetings The forward work programme of the Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee sets out the work which the Committee is intending to carry out in the following weeks and months. Any documents published indicate the current intentions of the Committee at the time of publishing, however the programme may change at any time to respond to external events. Type: For information First published: 15/06/2026 Consultations Priorities Consultation: Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee (running until 18/09/2026) Topics Helpful Links Find a Member of the Senedd chevron_right Sign up to updates from Senedd committees chevron_right Senedd Now chevron_right Glossary chevron_right Related No results were found', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47634', '2026-08-04', '', '', '', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '', '', '', NULL, 98.0, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Consultation open', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee; consultation; consultations', 0, '2026-08-04T14:02:47.583055', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47634', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('db78ff660a9d03a48793', 'committee_transcript', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', 'I think one of the things, when it comes to poverty, that is often invisible is time poverty. I know that people who are working multiple jobs just to pay their bills don''t have time, for example, to find or cook healthy food just on the fly. So, whilst you''ve said a lot about reducing food poverty and the food strategy, I''d be really interested to look at how we improve the availability and affordability of healthy food for families in poverty. Diolch.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16247', '2026-09-23', 'Sarah Rees', '', '5196', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', '16247', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16247?startPos=1730&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.744994', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16247&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771152', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dc1b24e8d5f32dd5b012', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', 'So, I think the first thing—. I might pass on to Tom in a second, to talk a little bit about some of the work that we do with partner organisations to share information and get information out to particular groups. The first thing to say would be that, obviously, local authorities and EROs, working with their partners in those authority areas, are going to be best placed to know and understand exactly where those harder to reach groups are likely to be. What we can do is provide them with some more support, some resources, some expertise, and the best ways to communicate information with those groups. We''ll be doing that, I think, ahead of the local elections next year. We''ve done some of that work ahead of the Senedd elections earlier this year, and we can provide that information so that local authority EROs can help deliver those messages most effectively. Tom, I don''t know if you wanted to say anything about the groups that we do work with already.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Tom Hawthorn', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=2002&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:48.992537', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769857', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dc589c078935ac5cb2a0', 'consultation', 'Senedd — committee consultation', 'Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 'Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee

This is an open Senedd consultation. Responding puts NRLA''s position formally on the record.

Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee, start date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 00:00:00 GMT, end date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:59:00 GMT

Closing date: 11 September 2026.', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgConsultationDisplay.aspx?ID=623', '2026-07-21', '', '', '', '', '', 'Senedd committee', '', '', '', '2026-09-11', 182.0, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'NRLA named', 'Consultation open', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee; closing date; consultation', 1, '2026-08-24T07:35:25.645068', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgRss.aspx?f=76', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dc626c3cd4a990c13103', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'I suppose I have some anxieties that there''ll be some authorities that—. I''m thinking of my old authority, Monmouthshire: a very small election team, and you couldn''t pick a worse set of elections to get it prepared for. If it was preparing for a Senedd election or a general election, it would be so much easier, wouldn''t it? But you''ve got so many candidates to sort out, so many people to get on board, there''s a lot of pressure on those teams as well. I''m a bit anxious, for a start, about where the additional staff are coming from. What skills do they need? How long will it take for them to be trained? That''s probably quite quick, I would imagine, but I don''t know. But all of those things that we talked about in the challenges that you had in Powys, can we really gear up to do it? Or is there even an opportunity where you can partially do it? So, you''re doing some of it, and you''ve just got to accept you''re only going to get so far on it. So, you bring so many people on, but that''s better than none, and then you sort of build on it. I mean, is there a hybrid? Does it have to be that you do it or you don''t do it, or can it be organic?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Peter Fox', '', '4787', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=6475&l=en', NULL, 97.7, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Opposition housing leads', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.614370', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769979', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dc85b2dea29037796709', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'Yes. I think that was the point I was going to come back to, because we''d had some difficulties. I raised with Darren Jones, who was a one-time Cabinet Office Minister, matters of the lack of co-operation from UK Government Ministries with their counterparts in the Welsh Government, and some of the practical difficulties that had arisen because of that. He was clear that that wasn''t the intention of the UK Government and sought to respond constructively and co-operatively to make sure that that didn''t happen. We stand ready as a Government, as a responsible Government, to co-operate as and when necessary with the UK Government, particularly on their legislation. Where those matters are minor and technical provisions, I mean, where those matters are engaged by the principles, then let''s co-operate. To do that effectively, we need to be there right at the beginning of the process, as we have been in some of the environmental regulations, and that''s worked well. I mean, if it can work there, there''s no reason for it not to work in other areas too.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dafydd Trystan Davies', '', '12140', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=3565&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.703775', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770453', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dca838f7a61550b2ab2c', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Thank you for that. You''re absolutely right, there is a responsibility on all of us to consider the multifaceted impacts that this kind of large infrastructure has. The environmental one is one in particular. You may be aware, of course, that planning policy reform, hopefully, is on its way, where the Government will be reviewing and updating national planning policy so that we can better enable some of these decisions to be done in a way that aligns all of these considerations that need to be taken on board when it comes to energy policy, the planning system, clearer spatial guidance, the environmental impact as well. So, it''s work in progress. It''s something we''re very mindful of and something we''re serious about addressing.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16084', '2026-07-08', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16084', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16084?startPos=3470&l=en', NULL, 27.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', '', '', 'planning policy; planning system', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:15.780720', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16084&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#766900', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dcbbae179d5861801e1b', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Finance', 'Thank you. You''ve spoken about cuts, but not taxes. However, actions speak louder than words. From April, the Welsh Government has introduced a higher business rates multiplier for larger premises. Is this the direction that you think this Government is going to go towards in dealing with the financial issues? Are you considering other tax rises, including income tax?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16261', '2026-09-16', 'Cai Parry-Jones', '', '12174', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Finance', '16261', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16261?startPos=3964&l=en', NULL, 60.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'business rates', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:17.048966', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16261&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769545', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dd3657adf9f154d165c5', 'calendar', 'Senedd forward look', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee — 16 September 2026, 09.00', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee is scheduled to meet on 16 September 2026 at 09.00.
Meeting status: Confirmed
This is an opportunity to influence: committee papers and any call for written evidence are normally published in the two weeks beforehand.', 'https://business.senedd.wales/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=978&MId=16232', '2026-09-16', '', '', '', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '', '16232', '', '2026-09-16', 48.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee; written evidence', 0, '2026-08-04T14:04:40.408237', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgWebService.asmx#GetAllMeetingsByDate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dd57cadedfe369b92c2e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'As I''ve said, this is a supplementary budget. It does exactly that: it supplements a budget. This Government has honoured the previous Government''s budget to the decimal point in order to provide continuity of delivery for our public sector and other partners. We added to that budget, but took nothing away. As the people of Wales would have expected of us in this supplementary budget, we have sought to allocate funding available to us on the priorities they voted for in May''s election—on reducing NHS waiting times, on increasing affordable childcare, on tackling child poverty, on transport initiatives, and on a capital programme to improve school and hospital buildings and build new homes. I understand that Members, during the scrutiny of this budget, have sought to pursue the allocation of £344 million consequential funding for the debt write-off to English local authorities as a result of ALN historical overspends in England. This Government has sought to engage constructively on that issue.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=23080&l=en', NULL, 66.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'housing_supply; fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context; Planning & place', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'new homes; supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.479544', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767967', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dd7c9520c48eef613dff', 'committee_transcript', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', 'Thank you for the question. Yes, that package—the cost-of-living support package for local authorities—is something that provides support to all kinds of interventions that can help to tackle the support that is needed. It was related to support involving food in particular. So, we''re talking here about foodbanks, community cafes, cookery skills, projects that provide healthy, nutritious food to families on low incomes. And by the same token, we''ve also ensured with that package that it takes a preventative approach. Advisory services, services with community organisations that would be able to provide support and signposting for people that they seek to support, were an important part of that to try to prevent crisis rather than meeting demand, because there''s always a balance to be struck there. We have to respond to crisis, but we also need to look at the longer term picture, that we don''t just pour money into the support side, although that''s very important, but we also try to prevent families from going into crisis in the first instance.

 In terms of the point on the fact that we reflected in the way that the funding was allocated via local authorities, that was something that was factored in from the very outset. So, it wasn''t true to say that we were taking money away from any one place, it''s something that we incorporated into the way that we were going to allocate the funding from the outset. But, yes, poverty exists, as this committee will hopefully know full well, in every ward almost in Wales. It''s something that impacts everyone, but it impacts communities in different ways. And rural poverty, for example, is related to the fact that it costs more sometimes for people to be able to access advice services, or it costs more for organisations to get those crisis food packages out to communities. So, that hasn''t always been reflected in the past and we wanted to reflect it this time because we, as a Government, recognise that we have to serve every part of Wales. That isn''t to say that we don''t serve some areas that aren''t rural areas, but we are looking at that bigger picture of poverty across Wales and ensuring that the support that we provide reflects the differences between the different local authorities.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16247', '2026-09-23', 'Sioned Williams', '', '8670', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '2. General scrutiny session: Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Equality and Social Justice', '16247', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16247?startPos=1553&l=en', NULL, 74.8, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Sector bodies; First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.727536', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16247&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771136', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dd8084c811ded4362678', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '6. Statement by the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health: Priorities for Public and Preventative Health', 'Thank you to the Deputy Minister for her statement today. As Welsh Labour''s spokesperson, I welcome the cross-Government approach to preventative health, but I''m interested in what outcomes will be delivered for people across Wales. You''ve mentioned today the designated preventative departmental expenditure line within the Welsh budget for 2027-28, but I''m sure you''d agree, Minister, that it isn''t just the creation of the budget line itself that we should be focused on, but rather how people''s overall health and well-being will improve. I, like many others, challenge the Government to go beyond the process. We want to know what exactly will change and how success will be measured during this Senedd term.

 I''m glad the Deputy Minister mentioned two very effective interventions: screening and vaccinations. It''s good to hear the Deputy Minister supports the continuation of the national lung cancer screening programme, which was introduced by the Welsh Labour Government. I''m surprised there''s no mention today of the HPV vaccine. Since it was introduced in 2008, the HPV vaccine has reduced cervical cancer rates by almost 90 per cent in women in their 20s, and that has saved hundreds of lives every year across the UK. So, I''d like to know how the Government will engage with schools across Wales to encourage participation in vaccination programmes like this.

 Cervical screening also saves lives, and there''s work to be done to make that more accessible. So, I''d like to see the Government learn from areas where there have been increases in screening uptake. You did give one example of screening uptake best practice, but I think there have been some other ones, particularly in London, where GPs have adapted to offer appointments for their clinics that fit in with people''s work and family lives, such as on weekends and late evenings. So, I''d be interested to hear if you''ve been able to look into that.

 Encouragement to help break down stigma is also key to increasing screening uptake. So, I''d like to know how Public Health Wales is focusing screening delivery that is tailored to local communities, for instance consistent breast screening opportunities in each geographical area throughout the year to support local health board demand. There''s also work to be done engaging with businesses and organisations to support their workforce to attend all screening as a priority.

 Targeted communications and education is important, breaking down stigma for everyone, but specifically for those attending their first screening appointment. We all know the way people access information is changing, and I''d like to know how national screening programmes are adapting to fit into those communication methods to reflect this.

 Inclusion health is a globally recognised approach to address and prevent the health inequalities facing marginalised groups who struggle to access health services and experience far poorer health outcomes. We know that there''s a huge human cost to these inequalities, as well as a cost to public services such as blue light services, A&E and emergency inpatient treatment. A stark example is people experiencing homelessness who experience acute physical and mental health problems and die 30 years younger than the general population.

 There are some fantastic examples of inclusion health work led by Public Health Wales and services such as Cardiff and Vale inclusion service, and the partnership work between Ysbyty Gwynedd and Cyngor Sir Ynys Môn. However, this is often reliant on passionate individuals going above and beyond the remit of their roles, rather than inclusion health being prioritised, systematic and integrated with health services. Prioritising inclusion health is key to preventative health, as well as delivering significant savings to emergency health services. So, will you commit to making inclusion health one of your ministerial priorities, and consider developing an inclusion health strategy?

 Finally, we know that sport helps to tackle obesity and to prevent physical and mental health conditions. Professional and grass-roots sport clubs play a leading role, and their impact is far-reaching. They are trusted places at the heart of our communities. I''d also recommend to you the Fit Fans programme, which works across our football league clubs. In Plaid Cymru''s manifesto, you said you would invest in sports and physical activity as part of the preventative health agenda, and you''ve mentioned today your discussions with the Minister for culture and sport. However, any new work stream does need funding. The health minister couldn''t give an answer when I previously asked how much that investment will be and where the money will come from. So, can you, Deputy Minister, today tell us that? Diolch.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Jayne Bryant', '', '5038', '', '', 'Plenary', '6. Statement by the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health: Priorities for Public and Preventative Health', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=15485&l=en', NULL, 55.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'homelessness', 'Housing system', 'Opposition housing leads', '', 'homelessness', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:09.774790', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767924', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dd9100710bbe206bb872', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'There''s always learning and I think that coherence is important. It can be done across portfolios, certainly, because, obviously, there are bespoke responsibilities that have to come together when events happen. So, I don''t think we should presume that, because it''s more than one person, it can''t work. But there''s no harm at all in looking at that wider picture and sharpening it up where we think that''s appropriate. And again, that may well be a consequence of the summit that''ll be held on 22 October and a discussion I''m more than willing to have with my colleagues in the Cabinet.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=2756&l=en', NULL, 34.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:34.696110', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771978', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('df07bd8ba5ef7ac384c1', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Trefnydd, Chief Whip and Cabinet Minister for Culture and Sport', 'I''m grateful for that response. Of course, at the other end of the spectrum, it''s vital that the Welsh Government is building a pipeline of sporting talent, and that, of course, means investing in sports facilities across the country. The financial challenges facing the sports sector are well known, and if the Welsh Government is serious about creating legacies from major sporting events, then the sector will need more funding. Now, your party''s own manifesto commits to increasing funding for culture and sport year on year throughout this Senedd term. So, Cabinet Minister, can you provide a guarantee to the culture and sports sector that they will receive a real-terms increase in the upcoming draft budget and every other year under this Government? And can you also provide an update on your audit of community and regional sporting facilities, so that we can better understand where capital investment needs to be targeted going forward?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16261', '2026-09-16', 'Paul Davies', '', '145', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Trefnydd, Chief Whip and Cabinet Minister for Culture and Sport', '16261', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16261?startPos=1318&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'draft budget', 0, '2026-09-17T11:56:12.640591', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16261&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769453', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('df54208cd63924d54660', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', 'Yes. You''ve got me again, I''m afraid. [ Laughter .] I just wanted to explore a little bit more about the notification period to opt out. I know that you were recommending a significant reduction in the notification period and are comfortable with a 28-day period. We know that, originally, the regulations were allowing for 45 days and then a—. Well, it was me, actually; I think I helped to encourage the Government to adopt 60 days for the pilots. I wonder if you could break that down a bit—why you believe, then, that there is a benefit for the 60-day reduction, and perhaps give some of your thinking around the time frames that you''re suggesting.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Peter Fox', '', '4787', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=632&l=en', NULL, 97.7, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Opposition housing leads', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:48.782676', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769832', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('df9a2b38c24dc0b3321e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'I ask Members to vote for this budget motion, to lift our collective heads above tribal party politics. Because this is a progressive budget for progressive parties. And even more importantly, it puts the priorities of the people of Wales first.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26453&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.861298', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767978', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dfdf5b3e24715359b7e1', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'I think the point that it brings out, which has come through the other questions as well, is those individual issues are—. The registration teams are skilled and capable of managing those and, spending that time having overseen a registration team with a high university population, they were very good at making sure there are additional things in place to make sure we didn''t miss those.

 It''s the cumulative effect of doing absent voters, overseas voters, of doing people who''ve got high churn, in a quick timescale, I think, which is probably the biggest area of risk to manage in this particular time frame. Over a longer time frame, in terms of future elections, I think that all becomes more manageable. So, I think the large risk rise is in the current situation, with the implementation for 2027, with all of those factors that are sitting with electoral registration teams. They are manageable, but they need really tight management, and reviewing how that''s gone is probably critical because of the fact that it''s the first time and, also, those delivery risks are not insignificant.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Ian Bancroft', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=5266&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.392077', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769962', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e02eacbeac70c653e3e1', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'Wildlife.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Elfyn Llwyd', '', '12193', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=5286&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:10.073664', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770554', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e0545199789dd18e4252', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '4. Statement by the First Minister: Legislation', 'It''s great to see that this Government is tackling the housing crisis, supporting housing affordability and increasing the rights of renters. In 2025, in my constituency, over 65 per cent of the population were priced out of housing in Gwynedd, and the median price on the Llŷn peninsula is more than £400,000, which is unaffordable for 96 per cent of local people. The impact this has on the area is very severe. Young people are leaving their localities, moving to the city or across the border, which greatly harms the local economy and culture. It''s good to see the Government doing this essential work, and I''m also really pleased to hear the news about the development of the right to adequate housing. This right is fundamental, and having a law on this would be transformative for thousands upon thousands of people across the country. So, what will the timetable be for bringing the aforementioned measures and the community right to buy to the Senedd?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Beca Brown', '', '12186', '', '', 'Plenary', '4. Statement by the First Minister: Legislation', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=10545&l=en', NULL, 137.5, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'rent_controls_and_affordability; homelessness; social_housing', 'Housing system; Private rented sector', 'Sector bodies; First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'adequate housing; community right to buy; housing affordability; right to adequate housing; right to buy', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:09.200293', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767768', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e0715bcbb3d1e1be1722', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '—in terms of the kind of main benefits we''ve identified, those would be them.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Tom Davies', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=856&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:48.815656', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769796', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e08df95acf606ac33c72', 'committee_transcript', 'Health and Social Care Committee', '2. General scrutiny session with the Cabinet Minister for Health and Care, the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health and the Deputy Minister for Social Care, Mental Health and Women’s Health', 'I think it''s important to note at the outset that these cancer targets and where we are with cancer isn''t where we should be. There are too many people presenting at hospital to receive a diagnosis far too late. There are too many people who feel lost in the system and that they don''t have clear communications when they are on a cancer journey and that after care. So, we have to see improvement, because, as you know better than I do, one in two of us will be in a situation where we are living with some kind of cancer in future. I think that we will be seeing figures published today that will demonstrate that things have improved somewhat in terms of that target.

 But the point—. You asked about targets; we''re reviewing the targets system as a whole at the moment. Health boards have several priorities and targets, and there is a view that there are too many of them, and we have to see whether it''s possible to decrease the number of targets and to make clear what our expectations are, instead of there being too many targets in the system. So, we are reviewing that at the moment.

 We would welcome and appreciate, truth be told, any recommendations that could be made, be they from the cancer community or from you here, on where we should look, because so much work is being done by the Government at the moment. The programme for government is going to be published; the 100 days has passed. A little bit of work like this, which would provide added value, is something that we would very much appreciate, and, I think, something that would be welcomed, because it''s not necessarily something that''s been factored in, in terms of cancer targets specifically, by us at the moment, because we are going to be developing a cancer strategy in due course and we''re going to try to improve quality and outcomes when it comes to cancer care. So, that''s something that should be looked at, and we would welcome it.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16251', '2026-09-17', 'Mabon ap Gwynfor', '', '269', '', '', 'Health and Social Care Committee', '2. General scrutiny session with the Cabinet Minister for Health and Care, the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health and the Deputy Minister for Social Care, Mental Health and Women’s Health', '16251', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16251?startPos=2128&l=en', NULL, 17.2, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'programme for government', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:14.172154', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16251&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770047', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e0a3022094ff1281cd32', 'oral_question', 'Oral Question', 'Oral Question - OQ64114', 'What action is the Welsh Government taking to tackle youth homelessness in Caerdydd Ffynnon Taf?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/OralQuestion/64114', '2026-06-04', 'Zaynub Akbar', '', '12141', '', 'Caerdydd Ffynnon Taf', 'Senedd (tabled business)', 'Tabled on 04/06/2026', '', '', NULL, 35.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'homelessness', 'Housing system', 'Other committee chairs', '', 'homelessness', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:46.897679', 'record_search:type=oral_question:query=homelessness', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e11123da97c725ae5303', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'Well, I do, indeed, and I''m giving you some latitude.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Irranca-Davies', 'Llywydd', '5053', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26304&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.843116', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767999', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e242f7858eef5345b38e', 'committee_transcript', 'Public Accounts and Public Administration Committee', '3. Introductory evidence session with the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'Cabinet Minister, on 8 June, you laid before the Senedd the legislative consent memorandum on the Public Office (Accountability) Bill. The Business Committee referred this to this committee and the Legislation Committee for scrutiny. What''s the Cabinet Minister’s understanding of the Bill’s timetable in the UK Parliament, the impact the timetable will have on the Senedd''s consideration of the LCM, and the related reporting deadlines?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16266', '2026-09-14', 'Andrew Griffin', '', '12187', '', '', 'Public Accounts and Public Administration Committee', '3. Introductory evidence session with the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16266', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16266?startPos=2400&l=en', NULL, 126.5, 'High', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context; committee_scrutiny', 'Context; Housing system', '', 'Legislative commitment; Opportunity to influence', 'LCM; Legislation Committee; evidence session; laid before the Senedd', 0, '2026-09-15T11:57:29.627140', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16266&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768584', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e24403ccc3f0e7a9d515', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', 'David, do you want to come in?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Carmelo Colasanto', '', '12152', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=6746&l=en', NULL, 103.5, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.656669', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770317', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e2ed9dc6bf2a1515267c', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '4. Statement by the Cabinet Minister for Finance: Rebalancing the non-domestic rates system', 'I''d point out here that Cardiff alone makes a net contribution of around £100 million to the Welsh national non-domestic rates pot. Will the Minister therefore share, in advance of the budget—today, if possible—the intended threshold for the higher multiplier, the number, type and location of the properties that will pay more, the average and largest expected increases, and her assessment of the effect on jobs, investment and prices? Can she also set out how she will avoid a cliff edge for businesses whose rateable value is just above £51,000?

 What these questions demonstrate, I think, Minister, is that what''s actually needed is wholesale reform of the business rates system in its totality. There was a commitment to that effect in Welsh Labour''s manifesto, just as there was in Plaid Cymru''s manifesto. I know that this new Government loves a review, it loves a commission. I wonder, Minister, if you could explain why your announcement today—welcome though it broadly is—is simply making tweaks at the margins and not getting into the more comprehensive changes that your party promised before the election. Our offer, as Welsh Labour, is to work with you so that we can make the system fair and so that we can incentivise businesses and local authorities to grow the value of NDR receipts and to drive wider economic growth. Thank you.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16260', '2026-09-15', 'Huw Thomas', '', '12156', '', '', 'Plenary', '4. Statement by the Cabinet Minister for Finance: Rebalancing the non-domestic rates system', '16260', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16260?startPos=10175&l=en', NULL, 60.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'business rates; non-domestic rates', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:26.112504', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16260&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769224', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e3093a9f405445539ed5', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Thank you for answering, Cabinet Minister. I know it''s in the Cabinet Minister for Enterprise, Connectivity and Energy''s portfolio. John.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'James Evans', '', '8585', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=5054&l=en', NULL, 46.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Other committee chairs', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:34.973315', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771842', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e32d5e6fc37a59cc5ea3', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '7. Reform UK Debate: The tourism sector', 'I did so for a very specific reason. Over 20 million people visit Cardiff every year, and we wanted to grow that number further, whilst also recognising and responding to the pressures that those visitors bring to the city. Over decades, Cardiff has built an enviable reputation as a destination for major sporting and cultural events. Every summer, the city teems with live music in our stadium, our castle and our parks. The new indoor arena, now under construction, will bring a further 1 million visitors every year to the city. From the Champions League final that Shav referenced to the Tour de France to the European football championship in 2028, a team Wales approach between Welsh Government, Cardiff Council and other partners has allowed Cardiff to secure some of the world''s premier sporting events over the years.

 I know from my unsuccessful attempt to purchase a ticket to see Oasis how much visitors are prepared to pay to purchase these golden tickets. If you''ve travelled from North America to see Taylor Swift, my guess is you''re not going to worry about paying a visitor levy of £1.30.

 Here''s the mad thing, for all the visitors that come to Cardiff, often as part of events that the council is delivering, for all the money they spend in local bars, restaurants, hotels, for all the overnight clean-up operations required after 70,000 people have partied in the Principality, the council receives not one penny of income, thanks to the completely centralised taxation system we have in this country. 

 A visitor levy, estimated to raise about £3.5 million a year for Cardiff, starts to change that calculation so that the council raises revenue from major events to in turn fund a better experience for visitors and residents alike. And it will also allow Cardiff to attract new events to the city and also better market ourselves internationally. That was the calculation in proposing a levy.

 In the extensive consultation carried out with key stakeholders and the general public, of the 2,000 responses received, 62 per cent supported those proposals, recognising how the money would be ring-fenced to support the visitor economy. It''s not a tourism tax, it''s an investment in tourism. It''s a modest contribution from visitors towards services, infrastructure and attractions that make Wales such a desirable place to visit in the first place.

 Elwyn Vaughan references—', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16084', '2026-07-08', 'Huw Thomas', '', '12156', '', '', 'Plenary', '7. Reform UK Debate: The tourism sector', '16084', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16084?startPos=14092&l=en', NULL, 82.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open', 'consultation; tourism tax; visitor levy', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:16.987798', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16084&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767117', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e34f8e492c1184fbc8ce', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'It''s difficult when these events happen; there will be consequences that you have to manage as best you can. But I think what''s most in our gift is managing ourselves to a position where we minimise the likelihood of those fires happening in the first place, because, once they''re burning, you can''t stop those kinds of emissions hitting communities. So what we need to focus on, I think, primarily is making sure that we minimise the risk from wildfires.

 There are two approaches to that. There''s the operational stuff—fire and rescue, the Welsh Government''s role, military support, all that kind of thing, and we can talk about that. But then we do have the longer term strategic interventions that we need to plan now, such as encouraging land management in a way that helps mitigate some of these risks. We already have certain sources of funding available to farmers—for example, when you think of drought, to look at sinking additional boreholes, creating lagoons for water et cetera. The sustainable agricultural loan scheme as well is out there to help farms become more resilient in the face of climate change, and maybe help some of these. We''re looking at doing more to encourage drought-resistant crops, which retain more moisture in the ground, through the sustainable farming scheme. There''s work ongoing on peatlands, for example, and rewetting, which can all help avoid finding ourselves in those situations. But when it does happen, then clearly there are public health consequences.

 Again, I''ll defer to Rhodri in relation to the Act, because I think those are circumstances or situations that arise that maybe hadn''t been considered at the time of the Act particularly, but obviously they would be relevant in terms of protecting people''s health.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=489&l=en', NULL, 34.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:34.343379', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771763', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e3780ecf3a9e4ced40f1', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Health and Care', 'So, the issue with the graduates lies squarely on the shoulders of the previous Government. This is an issue that was under your watch, back in 2023. As you said, these students were the cohort going through from 2022-23, and it will take a few years to work through the system. That''s why one of the first things that I did when I came into this post was set up a graduate summit, in order to try and find options for as many of these young people as possible. Because here in Wales, different from England, they are streamlined, so a promise is made to them. So we need to try and honour that promise, and it''s disappointing that we were left in a position where those promises were broken by the previous Government. So now we''re trying to find a long-term solution for this. That''s why we''ve asked Healthcare Inspectorate Wales to work with the health boards, to work with the representative bodies, to bring that plan together, and I expect to see a plan by the end of December—or early autumn, in fact.

 Now, when it comes to the bursary scheme, once again, may I just remind you that this wasn''t part of any negotiations that you brought forward or discussions that you brought forward for the supplementary budget, which you voted against as a party, in order to improve health outcomes in Wales. I am absolutely more than happy to discuss any options that you might have and consider their impact and assess how they might be included, but I just remind you that, as we have been informed by the Cabinet Minister for Finance, there are massive in-year pressures currently in the health service, and those pressures are only going to get worse as time goes on because of settlements coming down from London and the fact that we don''t have a fair funding formula for Wales.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Mabon ap Gwynfor', '', '269', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Health and Care', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=1214&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:04.785911', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768044', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e3c699522246c1fccead', 'committee_transcript', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'No, no, I was going to support the Counsel General. Also, when we talk about training future lawyers in our law schools, whether that''s in Aberystwyth University or even in Cardiff University, there are opportunities, aren''t there, to ensure that the Welsh language is an integral part of the law of Wales, that that is clear, and that students study the texts in Welsh and write their essays in Welsh on those issues. That is our world view and that is what we would like to see developing.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dafydd Trystan Davies', '', '12140', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=4562&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.889758', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770586', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e3f2a43362df62e27830', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '6. Member Debate under Standing Order 11.21(iv): Young people and employment', 'Well, where do I begin? I''m just really pleased that we''ve had such a good discussion and I just want to first of all really welcome the comments by the Minister. You found me nodding away and I was clearly in a lot of agreement with what you were saying, because the truth of the matter is that we have had a range of different schemes. Some of them have worked and some of them have still had gaps, whether those are the ones that we created here in Wales or whether they were created elsewhere.

 The big thing for me, in and amongst everything that I''ve heard from everybody, particularly the younger Members of the Senedd, is that we need to understand that this is about the social and economic issues and bringing them together. If we are not going to be doing anything very real in relation to building more homes that are affordable, addressing the issues around renters'' rights, for example, if we are not going to be tackling the big stuff around climate change and so forth, there isn''t going to be a future for anyone. And I worry, more often than not, about my own children, and even when I was first even considering having children, I was thinking, ''Am I doing the right thing?'' And now I look at my kids, one’s 15 and one’s 13, and I''m thinking, blimey—. Now I get to be in this building. And my daughter keeps reminding me, ''Mum, it''s because of you lot that we''re in this situation.'' So, I get it from home on a daily basis, so when I walk in—. Look, for me, what I would say, and I''ll ask the Minister, is: can you please report back to the Senedd after the discussion that you have with Milburn? Many people that I have spoken to, from lots of different organisations, including the TUC themselves, have said that it''s good that we''ve had that review, but there were still gaps even there. And I think that there''s clearly more work to be done.

 I just want to say there have been lots of comments made about immigration, and we can talk about these things all day long, but the data doesn''t stack up. And I think that I very much do welcome the fact that we have also heard, of course, from Janet, who made it very clear it''s about business rates. And I agree. We need to review business rates. There''s more work that needs to be done there. Actually, immigration has been a good thing for both Wales and for the country as a whole.

 What I would say is that, in terms of public procurement, specifically—', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Shav Taj', '', '12175', '', '', 'Plenary', '6. Member Debate under Standing Order 11.21(iv): Young people and employment', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=11645&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', '', '', 'business rates', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.848706', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768304', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e4307785efdb21b0f4eb', 'committee_transcript', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Just really quickly, Cabinet Minister, on that point, I was going to ask about a date when we think that report—. I agree with the chief veterinary officer that there’s no one-size-fits-all model to dealing with this, but it would be quite useful to have some assurances from the Government as to when that report is going to land, because it has been a long time in the making to get to here. And I know it''s got to be done right and I appreciate that, and it has to be done, and there has to be agreement on the board as well to what is published, but it would be quite useful if you could write to the committee to outline when that will be reported so we can put it into our programming.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'James Evans', '', '8585', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=6140&l=en', NULL, 46.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Other committee chairs', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:35.115240', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#772135', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e4513bc82c96a5106bc2', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', 'As you update ''Planning Policy Wales'', can you confirm your intention, therefore, to make the planning system more permissive so that we can build the homes Wales needs and, indeed, build the industrial developments that Wales needs? Will you make it more permissive, or will you continue to risk letting the not-in-my-backyard brigade stop developments and delay developments that have overwhelming public benefit?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Huw Thomas', '', '12156', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=5161&l=en', NULL, 60.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', 'Housing minister', '', 'Planning Policy Wales; planning policy; planning system', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.188393', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768184', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e532f3505b8b9c538f81', 'committee_transcript', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', 'Yes. Diolch, Gadeirydd. I wanted to go back to part of Peter''s question and ask about those harder to reach groups of people or communities, specifically those who are transient. I know we''ve discussed students, but I''m less concerned there, because, more broadly speaking, students will have a place of home and a place of study. I wanted to ask specifically about people who are homeless and people who are part of the Roma, Gypsy and Traveller communities, where there may be more movement than you typically find with students. Are you satisfied that enough outreach has happened to those types of communities who are more transient than students?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Elyn Stephens', '', '12164', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 1', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=1954&l=en', NULL, 132.2, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'homelessness; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'LGHP Committee members', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session; homeless', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:48.985246', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769854', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('e5aae1dc1412353e94e9', 'consultation', 'Welsh Government — Consultation', 'Regulations for designating Building Safety Authorities', 'Regulations for designating Building Safety Authorities
